	COMMAND OPTIONS
/W	WAIT FOR CR BEFORE OUTPUT
/S	STOP AND WAIT FOR CR AFTER EACH PAGE
/P	PARTIAL PRINTOUT: USER WILL BE PROMPTED FOR
	  PAGE NUMBERS FROM AND TO, DEFAULTS ARE 1
	  AND LAST PAGE.
THE CONSTRUCTION 'N IN THE FOLLOWING LIST INDICATES A
SYMBOLIC PARAMETER--THE ' DOES NOT APPEAR IN THE COMMAND.
HENCE, .TB'N MIGHT BE REPLACED BY .TB6.


	IN TEXT COMMANDS
COMMAND	DEFAULT		MEANING
_______ _______		_______
.BP		BEGIN NEW PAGE (IMPLIES BREAK)
.BR		BREAK (BEGIN NEW LINE)
.CE'N	N=1	CENTER NEXT N LINES
.DS	NO	DOUBLE SPACE
.EP'N	N=1	OMIT N PAGES (SKIP N PAGE NUMBERS)
.IN'N	N=0	INDENT LEFT MARGIN N SPACES
.LL'N	N=65	LINE LENGTH = N CHARACTERS
.NE'N	N=1	NEED N (2N IF DS) LINES REMAINING; ELSE
		  BEGIN NEW PAGE
.NL'N	N=66	NUMBER OF LINES PER PAGE, INCLUDING TOP
		  AND BOTTOM MARGINS (6 LINES EACH)
.NP		STOP PRINTING PAGE NUMBERS
.PF	NO	TYPE PAGE NUMBERS AT FOOT OF PAGE
.PF2	NO	SAME AS PF, BEGIN WITH PAGE 2
.PH	NO	TYPE PAGE NUMBERS AT TOP OF PAGE
.PH2	YES	SAME AS PH, BEGIN WITH PAGE 2
.RM		RESTORE MARGINS AFTER SQ'N (IMPLIES BR)
.SP'N	N=1	SPACE N LINES (IMPLIES BR)
.SS	YES	SINGLE SPACE
.SQ'N	N=0	SQUEEZE MARGINS N SPACES, EACH SIDE
		  (IMPLIES BR)
.TB'N	N=7	TRANSLATE TAB INTO N SPACES
.TR'AB		REPLACE EACH OCCURANCE OF CHARACTER A
		  WITH CHARACTER B
	DISCRETIONARY HYPHEN
	_____________ ______
	THE CHARACTER ^ WILL NOT APPEAR IN THE OUTPUT.
IF NECESSARY, IT WILL BE REPLACED BY AN END-OF-LINE HYPHEN,
AS AN AID TO JUSTIFICATION.
